  "id": "distribution",
  "term": "distribution",
  "definition": "In research methods, a distribution describes how often different values occur in a set of data. For observed data this is a frequency distribution, and for continuous data the values are usually grouped; distributions can also be represented by mathematical forms such as the normal distribution.",
